data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** The syntax is straightforward:

```csharp
Span<nint> nints = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

It works without `unsafe` context. On this 64-bit system, `nint`/`nuint` are 8 bytes each, with `nint.MaxValue` being `9223372036854775807` (Int64.MaxValue) and `nuint.MaxValue` being `18446744073709551615` (UInt64.MaxValue).
